<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR steady to softer on rate cut.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR steady to softer on rate cut.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly lower on Thursday following the two-percentage point drop in the Central Bank's overnight rate.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks offered lower swap rates after the Central Bank slashed its rates,&quot; a senior foreign bank trader said.</p>
<p>Traders said they expected Phibor rates to slide further for the rest of the week on beleif spot rates would ease again.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 May 29		  May 28</p>
<p>    1 W		13 13/16		14  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		12  5/8		 12 13/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11  9/16		11  5/8</p>
<p>    2 M		11  3/8		 11  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		11  5/16		11  3/8</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/16		11  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  1/8		 11  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		30-May		  29-May</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
